  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "• Preheat oven to 240°C/220°C fan-forced.\n• Cut zucchini and carrot into bite-size chunks. Slice red onion into thick wedges.\n• Place veggies on the lined oven tray. Sprinkle with Persian spice blend, season with salt and drizzle with olive oil.\n• Toss to coat and roast until tender, 20-25 mins.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/62738150d09888e7d806d456/step-0b6de37e.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Cut falafel into quarters. Zest lemon to get a pinch and cut into wedges. Drain sweetcorn.\n• In a small bowl, combine yoghurt, garlic aioli and lemon zest. Season to taste.\n• In a frying pan, heat oil (1/4 cup for 2P / 1/2 cup for 4P) over medium-high heat. Cook falafel until golden, 5-6 mins.\n• Remove pan from heat and drain the oil. Add honey and a squeeze of lemon juice to falafels, turning to coat.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/62738150d09888e7d806d456/step-4b50a573.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Meanwhile, in a medium saucepan, heat a drizzle of olive oil over medium\u0002high heat. Add sweetcorn and cook until softened, 2-3 mins. Add the water (see ingredients) and vegetable stock and bring to the boil.\n• Add couscous and the butter and stir to combine. Cover with a lid and remove from heat.\n• Set aside until the water has absorbed, 5 mins. Fluff up with fork.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/62738150d09888e7d806d456/step-e891b8b8.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Add the roasted veggies, baby spinach and a squeeze of lemon juice to the couscous. Toss to coat. Season to taste.\n• Divide roast veggie couscous and falafel between bowls. Top with lemon yoghurt sauce. Serve with remaining lemon wedges.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/62738150d09888e7d806d456/step-a678aaa6.jpg"
    }
  ]
